# Worker mobile — apps/worker-mobile

Copy from repo root `.env.example` or fill from `npx supabase status`:

```
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=<anon/publishable key>
```

# Stripe publishable key (client-safe). Never put sk_/rk_/whsec_ here.
# Sandbox TestFlight: pk_test_ + EXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PAYMENTS_MODE=sandbox
# Production: pk_live_ + mode=live (when enabled). Keep Supabase URL on Bridge-Hive.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PAYMENTS_MODE=sandbox


# Production / Preview builds — public Bridge Hive web origin for Auth emails:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_WEB_APP_URL=https://bridgehive.app
#
# When set to https://bridgehive.app (or www), password recovery uses:
# https://bridgehive.app/auth/confirm?next=%2Fauth%2Fworker%2Freset-password
# If unset, native fallback is:
# bridgehive://auth/worker/reset-password?source=recovery
# Never use localhost in production builds.

# Android Google Maps (Maps SDK for Android) — build-time only, read by app.config.ts.
# Set on EAS (preview + production environments), not as EXPO_PUBLIC_*.
# Restrict the key to package com.bridgehive.worker + signing SHA-1s.
# Without it, Android shift pages show the address/directions fallback instead of a map.
# iOS uses Apple Maps and needs no key.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_API_KEY=

Never put the service-role key or Stripe secret/webhook keys here.
